                <head>Report by Lieutenant Colonel Harold B. Hoskins on the situation in the Near
                    East</head>
                <p>[For summary of report, concerned preponderantly with the Arab-Zionist
                    controversy in Palestine, see <ref target="#pg782">page 782</ref>. For
                    correspondence on the dispatch of Lt. Col. Harold B. Hoskins on a mission to the
                    Near East, see <ref target="frus:frus1942v04/pg_24">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1942, volume IV, pages
                        24</ref> ff. See also <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg747">pages 747</ref>–<ref target="#pg751">751</ref>, <ref
                        target="#pg756">756</ref>–<ref target="#pg757">757</ref>, and <ref
                        target="#pg796">796</ref>–<ref target="#pg827">827</ref>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">passim</hi>.]</p>
            </div>
